---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="Zagros — Shared security knowledge for your team’s AI agents" description="Zagros is a self-hosted security knowledge service that gives teams and AI agents one shared reference built from authoritative security sources with preserved provenance.">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="status"><span class="dot"></span>self-hosted · shared · evidence-backed</div>
        <h1>Trusted security knowledge for your team’s AI agents.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Run one Zagros instance on infrastructure your team controls and give developers, AI agents, IDE integrations, and internal tools the same security reference. Zagros keeps source and provenance attached to the evidence your agents use.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero-art">
        <img src={`${base}zagros.png`} alt="Zagros — octopus over mountains, MCP shield" width="340" height="340" />
      </figure>
      <div class="cta-row hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${base}install/`}>Install Zagros</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}install-prompt/`}>AI install</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://codespaces.new/siamakhaz/Zagros?quickstart=1">Try live ↗</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${base}docs/`}>Docs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Why Zagros</div>
    <h2>One trusted reference. Shared across your team.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Instead of every AI agent searching independently or relying only on model memory, connect them to the same team-controlled security knowledge service.</p>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Team controlled</h3>
        <p>Run Zagros on infrastructure you control and decide how your team reaches it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Authoritative sources</h3>
        <p>Build the shared reference from established security sources such as CVE, MITRE, and OWASP.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Made for AI</h3>
        <p>Connect compatible agents and internal tools through MCP so they can retrieve the same evidence consistently.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Evidence with provenance</h3>
        <p>Keep source information attached to retrieved records so agents can preserve citations and verify important claims.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">How it works</div>
    <h2>Sources in. Shared evidence out.</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="n">1</div><div><h3>Collect trusted security knowledge</h3><p>Zagros ingests supported security sources into a team-controlled store.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">2</div><div><h3>Keep one shared reference</h3><p>Your team operates one Zagros service instead of maintaining separate knowledge copies for every agent or tool.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="n">3</div><div><h3>Connect the tools your team already uses</h3><p>AI agents, IDE integrations, and internal applications can query Zagros through MCP, CLI, or the web interface.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">Self-hosted</div>
    <h2>Your infrastructure. Your access boundary.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Zagros supports local use, but its primary deployment model is a shared internal service. Keep HelixDB private and place shared MCP/UI access behind your organization’s authenticated gateway, reverse proxy, VPN, or zero-trust network.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-primary mono" href={`${base}install/`}>Install Zagros →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}docs/deployment/`}>Deployment guide →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="kicker">For AI agents</div>
    <h2>One shared reference for many agents.</h2>
    <p class="sub">Zagros exposes its security knowledge through MCP so multiple agents can retrieve evidence from the same controlled corpus. Zagros provides retrieval and provenance; the consuming agent remains responsible for interpretation and recommendations.</p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content:flex-start">
      <a class="btn btn-primary mono" href={`${base}install-prompt/`}>AI install →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}docs/mcp/`}>MCP reference →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost mono" href={`${base}demo/`}>See the demo →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Base>
